  {
    "episode_id": 75136,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75136.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "No infrastructure is critically important. It's one of the highest priorities coming out of this Congress. And as a St. Louis County Minnesota commissioner, I was a chair of public works and transportation for two years. And we were responsible for 6,000 lane miles and over 300 bridges that we were responsible for. And what we did, we enacted a half percent sales tax that went directly to roads and bridges for 20 years. And it's paying off greatly in northern Minnesota. And we talk about there's no roads that are democratic roads or republican roads. As my predecessor, Jim Oberstar talks about their roads for us all.",
