  {
    "episode_id": 75136,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75136.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "You know, we'll have to wait and see. We just put it forward. It's got a really good chance of moving both in the House and the Senate. So I'm looking forward to those discussions, but the bottom line is when we invest in our infrastructure, We have an obligation to make sure that we're using the taxpayers' money wisely, and this is exactly what the paid act does.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "We just put it forward.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "When we invest in infrastructure, we have an obligation to use taxpayers' money wisely.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "We will have to wait and see.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker is looking forward to those discussions.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "This legislation is consistent with what the PAID Act does.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "It has a really good chance of moving both in the House and the Senate.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Public trust in government spending requires accountability and fiscal responsibility.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The PAID Act defines responsible use of public funds in infrastructure investment.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes they are acting in the public interest by promoting this proposal.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Taxpayers expect their money to be used efficiently and effectively.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Legislative success depends on bipartisan support in both chambers.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 75136,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75136.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "It seems that it makes common sense to try to stretch your dollars as far as possible.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "It makes common sense to try to stretch your dollars as far as possible.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "People generally value financial prudence.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Common sense is a reliable guide for practical decision-making.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Stretching dollars refers to maximizing purchasing power with limited resources.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The listener accepts the premise that saving money is worthwhile.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "Financial constraints are a normal and expected part of life.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Agree / Align"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 75136,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75136.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "Of course, nobody's going to argue with that. We want to make sure that these investments are used wisely and they're implemented across this nation. From east to west, north and south, we have federal highways and bridges that need to be replaced. And we can't wait any longer. I was not elected by my constituents out of Minnesota's 8th congressional district to sit and not do anything.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Nobody will argue with the idea being discussed.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "We should ensure that investments are used wisely.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Federal highways and bridges across the U.S. require replacement.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Investments should be implemented nationwide.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Immediate action on infrastructure repair is necessary.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The speaker's constituents expect active leadership and tangible outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Infrastructure investment is a legitimate and urgent national priority.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Delaying repairs leads to greater long-term costs or risks.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker has both legitimacy and responsibility to act on behalf of their constituents.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "National unity requires equitable distribution of infrastructure funding across regions.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 75136,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75136.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "You could also argue that whatever the final number is that comes out of Congress and gets approved by the President for any kind of infrastructure investment, that saving money on jobs just gives you more money to do more jobs.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
